  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only multi-profile with PCA n2000 + avgpool (config_002) is the clear best at 0.591 acc, while image-only ResNet50 (config_010) is very weak at 0.208 acc. Avgpool outperforms transformer (0.591 vs 0.519). The critical open question is whether multimodal fusion can improve upon the strong RNA baseline, given that the image signal from ResNet50 is extremely weak. Config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, PCA n2000, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) directly tests this: it pairs the best-validated RNA setup with the image modality using the simplest fusion mechanism. If concat fusion with a weak image signal cannot beat 0.591, it strongly suggests image (at least via ResNet50) is not contributing useful complementary information, redirecting budget toward RNA encoder exploration (scvi, scgpt). If it does help, it justifies investing in stronger image encoders (ViT-L) and more sophisticated fusion. This is the highest-information experiment because it resolves a fundamental architectural question (is multimodal worth pursuing?) before committing further budget to that branch."
}

